# The round-trip test (roundtrip_test.go) captures a bundle into
# testdata/roundtrip-scratch and removes it on cleanup. It is regenerated on
# every run and must never be committed: a committed copy would be discovered by
# TestSteelthread and run as if it were a real capture from a live session,
# which is the one thing a steel bundle is supposed to be evidence of.
/roundtrip-scratch/

# A bundle captured from a REAL session, dropped here by hand to check that it
# replays before deciding whether it can be committed at all.
#
# It has to live under testdata/ rather than in a temp directory, because a
# bundle's agentDir is "testdata/<name>" and the harness resolves it relative to
# this package's working directory — a capture anywhere else boots no fixture.
# So the safe place is one git cannot pick up.
#
# It is ignored because a live capture is the one artifact that must be READ
# before it is committed. A real session's tool output is whatever the tools
# returned: customer names, hostnames, internal identifiers, anything the agent
# was looking at. The secret scan proves the absence of known credential VALUES
# and says nothing about any of that. Capture into here, replay, read the
# bundle, and only then decide.
/livecapture-scratch/
